    ["page_layout_files",
    ".CSZ",
    "Cornerstone Document Template",
    "2.5",
    "A CSZ file is a document template created by IDEXX Cornerstone, a veterinary administrative management application. It contains a default document layout that includes various elements, such as text input fields, checkboxes, tables, images, and bookmarks. CSZ files are primarily used to create medical notes and client correspondence with similar formatting. Cornerstone is an application that assists veterinary clinics in various administrative tasks, such as scheduling appointments, tracking inventory, reporting, invoicing, and diagnostic integration. Document templates allow users to create reusable documents for saving data entry time and maintaining consistent content among staff members. To create a CSZ document template with Cornerstone follow these steps: Select Documents → Templates in the Lists menu. Click New, select Document template or Text only template. Select Edit Properties to set the properties of the template. When you are finished setting the properties, click OK to save the template and leave the Cornerstone Editor. You can also select Save or Save As to save the template but remain in the Cornerstone Editor. You can only open CSZ files with IDEXX Cornerstone. To open the CSZ file with Cornerstone, select Import Document Templates in the Tools menu, navigate to the location of the CSZ file, then click Import Template. Windows IDEXX Cornerstone.",
    "Windows IDEXX Cornerstone.",
    "?"],
    ["page_layout_files",
    ".VPD",
    "Visual Paradigm Online Diagram",
    "2.5",
    "3D model file used by MikuMikuDance, a dance and rhythm synchronization game; saves bone positions for a characters model, which give it a pose; can be used in a series of poses that make up a dance animation (.VMD file). Windows MikuMikuDanceFree. A VPD file is a diagram created by the Diagram app module available with Visual Paradigm Online. It is saved in the Visual Paradigm Online Diagram (VPD) format and contains diagram elements, such as activities, shapes, images, graphics, and text. VPD file open in Visual Paradigm Online Visual Paradigm Online is the online counterpart to the desktop Visual Paradigm software. The tool allows you to design various artwork and documents, such as diagrams, posters, flyers, infographics, and greeting cards. After saving a design, you can re-open it with Visual Paradigm Online to continue modifying the design. When saving it, you can choose the location where to save it, including the Visual Paradigm online storage space, Google Drive, and local storage on your device. Visual Paradigm Online saves artwork in different formats depending on the app modules you are using. For example, if you create a design with the Graphic Design app module, Visual Paradigm Online saves it as an.ART file. However, if you create a diagram with the Diagram app module, Visual Paradigm Online saves it as a VPD file. How to create a VPD file To create a VPD file: Select File → Create New Design the diagram Select File → Save as.. Name the file and choose the save location (Google Drive or Device). You can open a VPD file with Visual Paradigm Online in a web browser. To open a VPD file, select File → Open. Web Visual Paradigm OnlineFree. Database file created by VoxPro, an audio recorder and editor; contains metadata about the contents of the folder its held in, which is retrieved and displayed by VoxPro. You can manually rebuild VPD files that may be out of sync with its folder contents by selecting File → Rebuild File Database. Also, VoxPro will identify any out-of-sync or deleted VPD files and update or recreate them automatically. NOTE: Audion Labs was acquired by Wheatstone Corporation. VP_EMap.vpd - Default database file contained in every folder of every user account in VoxPro. Windows Wheatstone VoxPro.",
    "Windows MikuMikuDance. Web Visual Paradigm Online. Windows Wheatstone VoxPro.",
    "Visual Paradigm Online can convert VPD files to the following image formats:.PDF - Portable Document Format.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics File."],
    ["page_layout_files",
    ".DMTEMPLATE",
    "Direct Mail Template",
    "2.5",
    "Email template used by Direct Mail, an email marketing program used for sending advertisements; stores the graphics, layout, and text for an email; used for producing professional looking emails. Several templates are included with the Direct Mail installation. Mac e3 Software Direct Mail.",
    "Mac e3 Software Direct Mail.",
    "?"],
    ["page_layout_files",
    ".SPUB",
    "Swift Publisher Document",
    "2.5",
    "CD/DVD label or jewel case insert created with Disc Cover software; allows covers and labels for CDs and DVDs to be created easily and accurately printed; SPUB files may also be label or cover templates included with the software program. Disc Cover is developed specifically for Mac OS X and can import data from the Finder, iTunes, iPhoto, and iDVD. Mac BeLight Software Disc Cover. An SPUB file contains a document created by Swift Publisher, a page layout program for macOS. It stores information about the document in a proprietary format, which includes the page layout settings and document elements, such as text, images, and shapes in the document. SPUB files may be used to save various types of documents, including fliers, newsletters, announcements, booklets, brochures, calendars, posters, and business cards. SPUB file open in BeLight Swift Publisher 5 To create Swift Publisher documents, you can start with one of the many templates provided with the software or create one from scratch. To create an SPUB file in Swift Publisher, select File → New.., then choose a blank document or a template to create. After modifying the document, select File → Save to create the SPUB file. To open an SPUB file in Swift Publisher, select File → Open.. or Open Recent. To convert an SPUB file to another format, such as.PDF,.EPS,.TIFF,.PNG or.JPG, select File → Export.. in Swift Publisher. Mac BeLight Swift Publisher.",
    "Mac BeLight Software Disc Cover. Mac BeLight Swift Publisher.",
    "?"],
    ["page_layout_files",
    ".PA",
    "Print Artist Project",
    "2.5",
    "A PA file is a compressed archive created by ConeXware PowerArchiver, a utility used to compress, encrypt, and back up data. It stores one or more files compressed with the Advanced Codec Pack (PA) format, which includes various advanced filters and codecs for optimizing compression based on the file type, and may include FIPS 140-2 256-bit AES encryption. PowerArchiver users compress files as PA archives to save space for storage or transportation purposes and secure sensitive information. PA file open in ConeXware PowerArchiver 2022 ConeXware PowerArchiver is a utility for compressing, encrypting, and backing up data in Windows and macOS. The utility supports over 60 archive formats, besides the PA format, including.ZIP,.RAR,.7Z,.LZH,.GZIP, and.ARC. PowerArchiver Advanced Codec Pack Format ConeXware introduced the PowerArchiver Advanced Codec Pack format when it released PowerArchiver 2017. The format features two optimized compression modes: 1) Optimized Fast for faster compression and 2) Optimized Strong for stronger compression. PowerArchiver uses the BWTS algorithm to mix data before AES encryption to better secure archives. This encryption method results in archives that are better protected than ZIP and 7Z AES archive formats. You can open a PA file with ConeXware PowerArchiver in Windows and macOS. To open a PA file, select File → Open Archive. Windows ConeXware PowerArchiver. Print project created with Print Artist, a graphic design program; typically designed from a template and may include custom graphics and text; may be a brochure, greeting card, calendar, scrapbook, poster, or other type of printable document. Windows Nova Development Print Artist. A PA file is a configuration file used by PulseAudio, a free sound server program. It is run at startup to specify how a users sound system is configured. PulseAudios primary PA file is named default.pa. PA file open in Microsoft Visual Studio Code PulseAudio is a program used to manage how a computer outputs audio. For example, you can use PulseAudio to mix several audio streams and output them using one audio device, or you can use it to change audios sample format or channel count. The program is available primarily for Linux, but macOS and Windows versions also exist. At startup, PulseAudio loads settings that define how a users audio system is set up from a PA file. In most cases, PulseAudio loads these settings from a file named default.pa, which is located at either ~/​.config/​pulse/​default.pa or etc/​pulse/​default.pa. When PulseAudio runs as a system service, it instead loads settings from etc/​pulse/​system.pa. NOTE: The Windows version of PulseAudio is no longer maintained. default.pa - PulseAudios default startup script. system.pa - PulseAudios system service-level startup script. PulseAudios PA files are plain text files, so you can open and edit them in GitHub Atom, Apple TextEdit, Microsoft Notepad, or any other text editor. For example, you can edit default.pa to specify a new default audio output device. PulseAudio will then use that new default device the next time you start it. Windows PulseAudio. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac PulseAudio. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux PulseAudio. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor.",
    "Windows ConeXware PowerArchiver. Windows Nova Development Print Artist. Windows PulseAudio. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac PulseAudio. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux PulseAudio. Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor.",
    "ConeXware PowerArchiver (Windows version only) can convert PA files to various archive types, including the following formats:.ZIP - Zipped File.7Z - 7-Zip Compressed File.TAR - Consolidated Unix File Archive.CAB - Windows Cabinet File.LZH - LZH Compressed File.RAR - WinRAR Compressed Archive.BH - BlakHole Archive."],
