    ["page_layout_files",
    ".STUDIO",
    "Silhouette Studio Document",
    "2.5",
    "A STUDIO file is a design project created by Silhouette Studio, a program used to design items that can be cut with a Silhouette electronic cutting machine. It contains a design, which may include shapes, images, text, lines, colors, gradients, patterns, and effects. STUDIO files also store design page settings, cut settings, and registration marks. STUDIO file open in Silhouette Studio 3 The STUDIO file was the primary file associated with versions 1 and 2 of Silhouette Studio. When you would create and save a design project, the STUDIO file was the default format used to store the design. However, with the release of version 3 of Silhouette Studio, the STUDIO file has been replaced by the.STUDIO3 file. The STUDIO file is still supported by version 3 of Silhouette Studio. You can also save your design as a STUDIO file, although this may leave some advanced features unsaved. Windows Silhouette Studio. Mac Silhouette Studio.",
    "Windows Silhouette Studio. Mac Silhouette Studio.",
    "?"],
